  "continuity": "Initial 164-case gate passed all 133 domain and 27 existing data/provider/native cases plus three of four new protocol cases. Only the new creation-event fixture failed: version10 and missing m.federate=false violate the existing version12 nonfederated protocol. Only this test fixture changed. All four corrected cases and quality checks pass on 8455 unchanged inputs; production stayed unchanged.",
  "evidence": [
    "History repository overloads retain original metadata without inventing published group binding/lease/request fields. Original creator framing differs from conversation creator and remains exact.",
    "Both room metadata paths seal/open the same seven group coordinates. Exact retained devices alone bridge original company/device cursors; fresh devices retain isolated namespaces. Missing-key, cancellation and interruption never invoke an unsafe fallback.",
    "Four new cases cover bidirectional adoption cursor continuity, company/group and device/room replay isolation, key errors/cancellation, original creator/content in all three read shapes, invalid ownership before I/O, stalled progress, foreign/plaintext events and provider failure.",
    "Actual Synapse legacy history alternates original/group metadata after provider restart, continues old company cursors, preserves original ciphertext/sender/device IDs, and exercises fresh original-room reads with published-path continuation. Existing native history/registration regressions pass."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No schema or DI graph change; native original-room lookup/fallback is not connected by this protocol commit.",
    "Opaque provider transport is not SDK Megolm decryption. Complete group sync and historical peer-key proof, metadata/push, Mobile adoption and native hard-parent recovery remain required.",
    "Group rollout disabled; all 54 PRD acceptance groups open. Live8b40/schema116 push on/SMTP off, normal phone28, Mobile product/hosted0b804cb2 and Starter9959c1d unchanged."
  ]
